// GlWorld3d — the WebGL2 3D subset (docs/webgl2-fallback-plan.md §3.6): the
// GL twin of world3d.ts's World3d CORE. Same verbs, same retained + mutable
// handles, same 28-float mesh instance packing and bucket keying — the GPU
// half swaps storage buffers + render passes for instanced vertex attributes
// + GL state (shaders3d.ts holds the GLSL ports and the depth/winding rules).
//
// WHAT'S IN (Tier 1 + 2 of the fallback plan):
// - Every primitive mesh factory (box…extrude/custom), bucketed by
//   (shape, params) exactly like the original — one instanced draw per bucket.
// - Live Mesh3d handles (pos/size/euler/color/alpha/texture/emissive/parent),
//   opaque vs translucent partition (blend pass after opaques, depth test on
//   write off, insertion order — the original doesn't sort either).
// - Directional sun + hemisphere ambient + distance fog + up to 8 point/spot
//   lights as uniform arrays (world.light() → live Light3d handles).
// - CPU frustum culling (math3d sphereVsFrustum) for every bucket — the GPU
//   cull + drawIndirect static path becomes "packed every frame, culled on
//   the CPU" here (static: true is accepted; it only changes counts).
// - Billboards (shared 2D atlas, camera basis, alpha cutout), blob shadows,
//   the full procedural sky (gradient/sun/clouds/stars/moon — sky3d's state
//   machine reused, the fragment shader ported), CPU particles (world.fx /
//   world.burst via particles3d, FX_WGSL ported).
// - OBJ/GLB models via the device-free model-data cache — one bucket per
//   material/primitive, standalone sRGB textures; rigged GLBs VS-skin from an
//   RGBA32F joint-palette texture (model3d's AnimatedModel3d mixes on the CPU
//   exactly as on WebGPU).
// - Terrain: heightfield chunks + the baked colormap as ordinary buckets
//   (no grass, no deform rendering — the CPU DeformMap still works for
//   gameplay heightAt).
// - CPU picking: screenRay + rayObbLocal per instance, same pick(e, opts)
//   promise shape (obb-tight, not pixel-exact — see pick()).
// - orbit()/follow()/lookAt/project()/screenRay() — the rig maths reused or
//   duplicated from the original verbatim.
//
// ALSO REAL on the fallback (promoted from the original stub tier):
// - 3D vector lines/wireframes (vector3d.ts CPU + the line GLSL port);
// - env/IBL reflections (CPU-mipped equirect, procedural or custom);
// - voxels + voxelEditor (voxel3d/voxeledit3d CPU reused; webgl3d/voxels.ts);
// - agents (agents3d.ts reused verbatim; gizmos through the line layer);
// - trails (webgl3d/trails.ts CPU duplicate + the TRAIL_WGSL port — instance
//   data rides an RGBA32F texture, 29 texels per trail);
// - emitter() as a capped CPU approximation over world.fx;
// - wisps (WISP_WGSL ported — vertex-stage noise twist/wind);
// - shadow maps (world.shadows(): depth-only ortho pass into a compare-mode
//   depth texture, 9-tap Poisson PCF ×2×2 HW PCF, uniform-gated — blobs and
//   the map stay mutually exclusive like the original);
// - sunScreen + lens flare (the ghost chain; occlusion via an async
//   ANY_SAMPLES_PASSED probe query instead of vertex-stage depth taps);
// - SSAO + god rays (setSsao/setRays — the renderer's depth-texture seam:
//   the scene renders offscreen, its depth is blitted to a scratch copy,
//   half-res estimate/march + composite land back on the scene FBO);
// - WATER (webgl3d/water.ts — the Water3d handle/presets/heightAt replica
//   reused from water3d.ts; grid Gerstner + ribbon streams, shore blend via
//   the depth copy, foam-stamp wakes, wells, Snell underside);
// - UNDERWATER (webgl3d/underwater.ts — the Underwater3d handle reused; fog
//   retarget, Beer–Lambert multiply + in-scatter composite, the ABZU shaft
//   ring, seabed caustics in the mesh shader).
//
// - GRASS (webgl3d/grass.ts — CPU lattice spawner replacing the compute
//   kernels; the blade geometry/wind/wrap-lit shading ported verbatim; the
//   far billboard cards + flowers are cut, see grass.ts);
// - SNOW-DEFORM terrain rendering (the deform mesh variant + the high-poly
//   snow-layer patch, base-parity shading; the CPU DeformMap uploads R32F
//   dirty regions each frame).
//
// - spot-light BEAM shafts (beam3d.ts ported — the volumetric cone layer,
//   soft-depth-faded via the depth copy);
// - WEATHER rain/snow: the emitter adapter's wrap+respawn recipes run as a
//   dedicated CPU pool (~4k drops, torus-wrapped) through the fx stream.
//
// REMAINING NOTICES (one console warn, never crashes): the CPU emitter
// approximation and the 8-light cap. Custom WGSL snippets don't run (by
// design — plan §1).
//
// COORDINATES: identical to World3d — y-UP, right-handed, +Z toward the
// camera, right-hand-turn yaw. All GPU objects rebuild from CPU state on
// context restore (the constructor registers with the renderer's onRebuild).

